\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-HK official says no plans to change  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  peg\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2012\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details on peg, background)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 2 (Reuters) - Hong Kong has no plans to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg against the U.S. dollar, a government official said on Friday, dismissing talk of the authorities rethinking policy after being forced into heavy sales of the Hong Kong dollar to curb its strength.\par \par \uc2 KC Chan, Secretary for Financial Services and the Treasury, asserted Hong Kong's commitment to the pillar of its monetary policy during a Legislative Council panel discussion on financial affairs and housing that was available via webcast.\par \par \uc2 "We have no plans to change the Hong Kong dollar peg," Chan said in response to a question from a legislator.\par \par \uc2 The 29-year-old peg has come under pressure recently, as the former British colony, along with other Asian centres, became favoured destinations for funds unleashed by major quantitative easing measures in the U.S., Europe and Japan.\par \par \uc2 During the past two weeks, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of $3.5 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars into the market via nine \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Established in 1983, and the last major change to the peg was in 2005 when the trading band was widened to allow the Hong Kong dollar to trade between 7.75 and 7.85 against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Under the peg, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits the upper or lower limit.\par \par \uc2 Back in June, Joseph Yam, an adviser to \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a former \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, suggested Hong Kong may want to consider ditch its exchange rate target, fuelling speculation that the peg might be abandoned.\par \par \uc2 However, most analysts believe the peg remains the most suitable system for Hong Kong for the time being, given the benefits of switching to another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime are unclear.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to expect the HKMA to maintain the integrity of the HKD peg and do all it needs to in order to keep the system intact," Paul Mackel, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research, said in a recent report.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong, a former British territory, returned to Chinese rule in 1997 but has kept its own distinct financial system. Many analysts expect the big change in policy will only happen when the yuan becomes freely convertible, in which case the Hong Kong dollar could be re-pegged against the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since it was adopted, the peg has survived a number of speculative attacks as well as regional and global financial crises, and authorities have continued to reiterate their commitment to the peg.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the most worrying aspect of the surge of funds into Hong Kong has been the effect on property prices, which have risen about 20 percent in the first nine months of this year, with even small and medium-sized units climbing some 21 percent.\par \par \uc2 Fearful of the social impact, the city introduced new measures to curb runaway prices last Friday, including a 15 percent tax on overseas buyers and an increase of the stamp duty on short-term transactions.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michelle Chen and Christina Lo; Editing by Anne Marie Roantree and Simon Cameron-Moore)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG-PEG/  (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | Z | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121102e8b20007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
