\par\par \b \uc2 HK Shares End Higher; Continued Fund Inflows, China PMI Boost Interest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeffrey Ng   \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2012\par 09:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--Robust manufacturing data out of China and continued fund inflows into Hong Kong helped boost the city's benchmark index Thursday, even as overnight declines on Wall Street and weakness in other Asian stock markets capped gains.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Hang Seng Index rose 180.05 points, or 0.8%, to 21,821.87, its highest close since Aug. 4, 2011, when the index ended at 21,884. The index recovered from a low of 21,506.05 early in the session after the release of China's official gauge of manufacturing activity for October indicated an expansion after two months of contraction.\par \par \uc2 Market volumes for the session totaled 58.70 billion Hong Kong dollars (US$7.6 billion), up from HK$47.94 billion Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Gains on Thursday added to the 1.0% rise the previous day, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second straight day to cap gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, signalling continued fund inflows.\par \par \uc2 If the last period of major liquidity inflows was any measure, there remains significantly more room for more hot money to flow into Hong Kong, said Francis Lun, managing director at brokerage Lyncean Holdings. For many months between 2008 and 2009, the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to defend the local dollar's peg to the greenback as liquidity poured into Hong Kong following the first round of U.S. quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 Now, "there's also a lot of speculative inflows betting on further gains in the Chinese yuan," said Mr. Lun, as the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has for years been seen as a proxy for the yuan's movements, which isn't freely convertible. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in recent weeks been rising against the U.S. dollar amid further signs of a steady recovery in the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The broker said the continued inflows will help further lift the city's benchmark index, forecasting the next resistance level at around 23,000 points.\par \par \uc2 Australia's benchmark S&P/ASX 200 closed down 1.3% at a four-week low, while South Korea's Kospi dropped 0.7% to 1,898.44. Overnight, the Dow Jones Industrial Average slipped 10.75 points, or 0.08% from Friday's close, to 13096.46, after two days of closures due to superstorm Sandy.\par \par \uc2 Blue-chip property stocks in Hong Kong rose further as they recovered more from Monday's declines, after the government slapped a tax on foreign residential property buyers.\par \par \uc2 "The rebound in the stocks show that investors aren't too worried about property prices coming down sharply from the measures, even if transaction volumes may fall," said Conita Hung, a director at \uc2 Delta Asia Financial\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among the real estate firms, New World Holdings ended up 0.8% at HK$12.08, \uc2 Wharf Holdings\uc2  rose 0.6% to HK$53.35, and Cheung Kong added 0.4% to HK$115.0.\par \par \uc2 Chinese shippers also outperformed the broad market, led by \uc2 China Shipping Container Lines\uc2  after brokerage Daiwa upgraded the stock to Buy from Hold. Daiwa revised its 2012 earnings forecast for China Shipping to a CNY41 million net profit, versus an earlier forecast of a CNY371 million loss. The house also raised its target price to HK$2.74 from HK$2.70. The stock jumped 8.2% Thursday to HK$2.24.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeffrey Ng at jeffrey.ng@wsj.com [ 01-11-12 0852GMT ]\