\par\par \b \uc2 ICBC-HKMA continues to curb HK dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2012\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 25102012\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) said Wednesday it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from exceeding the top end of the trading band with the U.S. dollar as strong demand is driving up the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the HKMA injected over 3 billion HK dollars (about 408 million U.S. dollars) into the market this morning, bringing the total amount to over 14 billion HK dollars since Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The move came as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 7.75 HK dollars to one U.S. dollar, the stronger end of the trading band under the \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Board Mechanism. The buying of U.S. dollars is triggered automatically when the exchange rate hits the upper limit.\par \par \uc2 Deputy Chief Executive of the \uc2 HKMA Eddie Yue\uc2  said there are various reasons in the recent spike in demand for the Hong Kong dollar, for instance, the latest round of monetary easing in the United States may increase demand for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , equities and bonds. Other investors who had previously held U.S. dollar assets may also switch back to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yue said he expects the high demand to persist, and the authority is obliged to sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its value from the peg range. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still remains stable against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Once the transaction is settled on Wednesday, the total balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA will reach 163 billion HK dollars. The HKMA said the increase is unlikely to affect the close-to-zero interbank rates in the short term.\par \par \uc2 The authority said it will closely monitor market developments and ensure the stability of the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 The last time Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a similar level was back in 2009, when the HKMA sold over 2 billion HK dollars on the market.\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020121026e8aq00068\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
