\par\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Keeps Up Heat on  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By FIONA LAW  \par \uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 02:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's banking system is awash in cash, pushing lending rates down and threatening to push up property prices, as the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold a combined 14.36 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars (US$1.85 billion) in four \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Friday as it seeks to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening out of its trading band against the U.S. dollar. The HKMA said Wednesday it expects funds will continue to flow into the Hong Kong dollar on a net basis "for some time" and pledged to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability.\par \par \uc2 Cash has surged into the banking system from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and as overseas fund managers, more willing to take on risk as a result of global stimulus measures, snap up the city's stocks. As a result, Hong Kong's benchmark three-month interbank lending rate has fallen to 0.25%, from 0.35% before the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and 0.5% two weeks ago. When that rate falls, it brings down benchmark borrowing rates for companies and mortgage rates for individuals.\par \par \uc2 Barclays said that if interest rates remain low, there will likely be more lending, which would support the property market. The city's housing prices have already risen 16% from the start of the year through to August. When borrowing rates fell even more dramatically, from 4% to below 1% in 2009, home prices jumped 29%.\par \par \uc2 Still, "the rates drop hasn't been drastic, and its impact on the financial market wouldn't be as substantial as it was during 2008-2009," said Tommy Ong, head of wealth-management solutions at DBS Group Holdings Ltd.'s Hong Kong unit.\par \par \uc2 A measure of liquidity among banks in Hong Kong, the so-called aggregate balance, has climbed to HK$163 billion, from around HK$149 billion before the first injection Friday in New York trade. The last time the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  was during 2008 and 2009, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was seen as a haven during global market turmoil. At the time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also boosted by the Federal Reserve's first round of quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 Eddie Yue, deputy chief executive of the HKMA, said Wednesday that the U.S. stimulus measures announced in September may trigger demand for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , equities and bonds. Some investors who have held U.S. dollars are switching back to the local unit as investors world-wide become more willing to take on risk, he added.\par \par \uc2 This time, the HKMA has been mostly stepping in during the U.S. day, when trading volume is less, making it easier for speculators to move the market if they wish to test the top end of the band. The Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade between HK$7.7500 and HK$7.8500 per U.S. dollar. Late Wednesday, the rate was HK$7.7505.\par \par \uc2 One-year forward contracts for Hong Kong dollars were priced at HK$7.7440 per dollar late Wednesday, a level beyond the strong end of the trading band. Still, few are predicting any quick change to the peg, which was created in 1983 as confidence in the former British colony wavered ahead of its handover to China in 1997.\par \par \uc2 "The cost of change is substantial, while the benefits are highly uncertain," said Robert Minikin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered PLC's Hong Kong unit. "Any change to the peg will be long-delayed until the yuan becomes fully convertible."\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan is seen as a possible hook for the Hong Kong dollar, as the city's economy is increasingly integrated to the mainland.\par \par \uc2 "But [yuan's full convertibility] will unlikely happen in the next decade," said Mr. Minikin.\par \par \uc2 Write to Fiona Law at Fiona.Law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120121025e8ap00003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
