\par\par \b \uc2 HK Shares End at Fresh 14-Month High; 10-Day Winning Streak\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Li   \par \uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 10:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--Hong Kong shares ended higher for the 10th straight session on Thursday, underpinned by investors' expectation of further fund inflows to the city, although profit-taking limited the benchmark index's upside.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Hang Seng Index rose 46.45 points, or 0.2%, to 21,810.23, its highest close since ending at 21,884 on Aug. 4, 2011. Overall, it has gained 4.3% over the last 10 sessions, bringing its year-to-date advancement to 18.3%.\par \par \uc2 Market volume totaled 61.25 billion Hong Kong dollars (US$7.90 billion), down from HK$68.65 billion Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "All eyes are on the Hong Kong dollar's strength. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stays near 7.75, the stronger end of its trading band (against the greenback), the liquidity-driven rally may continue on expectations of further fund inflow," said Castor Pang, research head at Core Pacific - Yamaichi.\par \par \uc2 At 0800 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.7504, still near the strong end of its trading band after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UOB KayHian said in a note that it believes the liquidity has been mainly attracted by the improved outlook of the Chinese economy and recent strengthening of the yuan.\par \par \uc2 The brokerage added that the benchmark index has already rebounded in the last few weeks, and that could be partly due to the anticipation of money inflows. "Hence, there may not be much upside unless there is plenty of hot money continuing to come in."\par \par \uc2 Cnooc rose 1.4% to HK$16.26, getting a fillip from its \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  update, during which China's largest offshore oil producer raised its 2012 net oil and gas output target to 335 million-345 million barrels of oil equivalent from its previous target of 330 million-340 million BOE.\par \par \uc2 Fashion retailer Esprit rebounded 1.1% to HK$11.38 after taking a 9.5% beating Wednesday due to its more than HK$5 billion rights issue plan. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said the size of the rights issue is "much larger than expected," and from the magnitude of the rights issue, "we think the management likely wanted to build a little extra buffer given limited visibility in the timing and trajectory of a more meaningful recovery."\par \par \uc2 Chinese names continued to succumb to profit-taking with Ping An, the country's second largest life insurer, falling 1.3% to HK$63.05. Port operator Cosco Pacific dipped 1.4% to HK$11.42 and China Mobile slipped 0.6% to HK$86.80.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Galaxy Entertainment rallied 3.6% to HK$25.95 to lead gains among Macau casino operators, after it said Thursday its adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization jumped 46% year-on-year to HK$2.6 billion in the third quarter, thanks to its new flagship resort in Macau.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Robert Li\uc2  at robert.li@dowjones.com [ 25-10-12 0859GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5013 55108   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121025e8ap000oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
