\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Weaken  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2012\par 03:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a further 3.062 billion Hong Kong dollars ($395 million) Tuesday in New York trade to weaken the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its fourth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a week.\par \par \uc2 The city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier sold 6.626 billion Hong Kong dollars ($854.9 million) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, while the city was closed for a holiday, according to the HKMA.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar hit HK$7.7500, the lowest limit at which the U.S. dollar is allowed to trade against the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85.\par \par \uc2 It is the fourth time the HKMA has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a week.\par \par \uc2 On Friday during New York trading hours, the HKMA sold $HK4.67 billion to push down the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen weeks of capital inflows driven by the U.S. Federal Reserve's latest round of stimulus measures and the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent pledge to buy sovereign bonds. Those moves have restored global investor confidence and led money managers to buy a wide range of assets around the world, including in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Write to Fiona Law at fiona.law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 10-23-12 2105ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020121024e8ao00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
