\par\par \b \uc2 HK Shares End at More Than 14-Month High on Liquidity Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Li   \par \uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2012\par 10:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--Hong Kong shares ended Monday at a more than 14-month high, spurred by expectations of more fund inflows to the city.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Hang Seng Index rose 145.79 points, or 0.7%, to 21,697.55, its highest close since ending at 21,884 on Aug. 4, 2011. The benchmark index remains below its 2012 intraday high of 21,760 set Feb. 20. Overall, the index has risen 3.5% over an eight-session winning streak.\par \par \uc2 Market volume totaled 51.08 billion Hong Kong dollars (US$6.59 billion), down from HK$56.39 billion Friday.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$4.67 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during New York trading as the U.S. dollar hit HK$7.7500, the upper limit of where the Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade against the greenback. This happened after weeks of capital inflows that have pushed up the value of the Hong Kong dollar, forcing the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in nearly three years over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 "Judging from past experiences, whenever this happens, the local stock market tends to have a solid performance afterwards," said \uc2 Alvin Cheung\uc2 , associate director at Prudential Brokerage. Mr. Cheung expects the Hang Seng Index's uptrend to continue until the month-end, with 21,760 as the short-term target.\par \par \uc2 That view was shared by ANZ Research, which said in a note that it believed "the strong inflow into the (Hong Kong dollar) money market relates to the recovery of global investors' sentiment towards \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market." It added that the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  "may foretell a rally of other asset classes, similar to the situation after the global financial crisis stabilized."\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong property stocks outperformed Monday, as the HKMA's liquidity injection was taken by investors as an indication of fund inflows.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said that the last time the HKMA bought the U.S. dollar to hold down the local dollar's value was in December 2009, and the result was a decline in domestic lending rates, most notably mortgage rates, a domestic credit expansion and a liquidity-driven rally in property prices. "If this persists, as in 2009, then we expect lower lending rates and a domestic credit expansion to support higher property prices."\par \par \uc2 Henderson Land rose 2.1% to HK$57.00, \uc2 Sun Hung Kai Properties\uc2  gained 1.0% to HK$109.10 and \uc2 Sino Land\uc2  was up 1.0% at HK$14.28.\par \par \uc2 Bourse operator Hong Kong Exchanges is another obvious beneficiary of liquidity inflows. It ended up 3.5% at HK$125.60 and was the best-performing blue chip Monday.\par \par \uc2 Macau casino operator \uc2 SJM Holdings\uc2  rose 0.6% to HK$17.10 after setting a 52-week high of HK$17.36 intraday, spurred by news that it received the Macau government's approval for the development of a casino resort in Cotai.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Robert Li\uc2  at robert.li@dowjones.com [ 22-10-12 0841GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5013 55108   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121022e8am000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
