\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: HK IPO Fever Boosts Local Rates, HK Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By David Roman   \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column   \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 06:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar is poised to rise in coming weeks toward the top end of its parity band against the U.S. dollar, driven by the latest rally in stocks and a jump in local rates on the territory's recent IPO fever.\par \par \uc2 That means the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon be forced to join Japan and other Asian countries in their efforts to control surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A continued slide in U.S. rates is the main reason for Hong Kong dollar strength. As the U.S. Federal Reserve hints that it will keep ultra-low rates in place until 2011 or even longer, interbank dollar rates used by commercial banks, or Libor, have tumbled to five-month lows.\par \par \uc2 That diminishes the appeal of carry trades where investors borrow in Hong Kong dollars -- normally at cheaper rates due to the territory's status as a banking hub -- and then buy U.S. dollars, capturing the spread between the two. A narrowing spread between local and Libor means such trades, traditionally a key source of greenback demand in the territory, are unlikely to be attractive anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 The spread rose to 0.3 percentage points in late May but after narrowing for weeks it turned negative Monday as the benchmark 3-month Hibor rate for Hong Kong banks rose to 0.32%, while the equivalent 3-month Libor rate dropped to 0.29%.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong traders say a flurry of initial public offerings expected in the territory in the next three weeks is behind the uptick in Hibor, which some expect may reach 0.4%. Meanwhile, Libor may fall further if the U.S. Fed expands its quantitative-easing policy as some expect.\par \par \uc2 Traders say Hibor rates should drop back below Libor once demand for Hong Kong dollars flags, as happened after an earlier IPO-driven Hibor spike in late June-early July. But Fed policies weighing on Libor rates mean spreads are likely to remain minuscule, discouraging carry trades in the US dollar and keeping the Hong Kong unit strongly supported.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeing central banks in the developed world flooding markets with liquidity, including the Fed," said Erik Lueth, a Hong Kong-based economist with \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 . "All that liquidity has to go somewhere, and it's going to Asia, places like Hong Kong."\par \par \uc2 RBS is forecasting that the U.S. dollar may fall to $7.7500 by the end of this month and stay there through year-end, from $7.7630 last. That means the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling additional \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars, Lueth added, something it hasn't done since December 2009.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA, which keeps the U.S. dollar pegged between HK$7.7500-HK$7.8500, flooded the market with Hong Kong dollars in 2008 and 2009 as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed near the low end of the parity band. That ended up feeding a property bubble in the territory -- and could well do so again.\par \par \uc2 (David Roman, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporter, has been a Dow Jones correspondent since 2002, covering economic and corporate news. He can be reached at 65 6415 4045 or by e-mail: david.roman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAsia@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 21-09-10 0447GMT ]\par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100921e69l000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
