\par\par \b \uc2 HK Exchange Fund may see loss on market volatility-HKMA\b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2010\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 22 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Exchange Fund may suffer some paper losses because of volatility in certain asset classes, the HKMA said on Thursday, amid a weak performance by the territory's stock market.\par \par \uc2 Europe's moves to implement fiscal austerity measures should also address investor concerns about the long-term financial health of European nations, HKMA Deputy Chief Executive Eddie Yue said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Surely we hope that investor sentiment could improve and the investment environment could become more accommodating in the second half of the year," Yue said. "But current uncertainties in the market are such that it is hard to take this optimistic view."\par \par \uc2 The Exchange Fund is tasked with backing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade when necessary. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar, but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\par \par \uc2 Foreign assets in the fund stood at HK$1.916 trillion ($245 billion) at the end of June 2010, up HK$0.9 billion from the month before, the HKMA had said on July 14. [ID:nHKF002509]\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's benchmark Hang Seng Index <.HSI> has fallen about 5 percent so far this year, weighed down by wider worries about a cooling Chinese economy. (Reporting by Kelvin Soh; Editing by Chris Lewis)\par \par \uc2 HKMA/FUND|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100722e67m000wo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\p