\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: HKMA: Yuan Flexibility Doesn't Affect HK Dollar/US Dollar Peg\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2010\par 10:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds trader, strategist's comments on outlook for the HK dollar, former HKMA chief's comment on yuan.)\par \par \uc2 By Chester Yung\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement over the weekend that it will increase the flexibility of its exchange-rate regime hasn't affected the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday, adding a stronger yuan will have a "modest" impact on the city's inflation.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the move by the People's Bank of China will place pressure on the U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar pair this week but \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was up sharply against the U.S. dollar Monday morning after the PBOC said over the weekend it would increase the flexibility of its exchange-rate regime, implying it would allow the yuan to resume its gradual rise against the U.S. dollar. The freely convertible Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is often traded as proxy for the yuan.\par \par \uc2 At 0820 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.721, down from HK$7.7856 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 However, a HKMA spokesman said: "We have no plan to alter the USD/HKD peg as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime has been effective."\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "I don't expect the U.S. dollar to fall back to the lower limit of the trading band in the near term as some market players are eager to buy back the U.S. dollar for bargain-hunting near the HK$7.76 level. There is no need for the HKMA to step in (to buy back the U.S. dollar) now," said a senior trader at a U.K. bank.\par \par \uc2 Patrick Bennett, chief strategist at Standard Bank, said: "The move in the U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar pair reflects the general move in U.S. dollar/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , of course led by the PBOC announcement."\par \par \uc2 He said as long as the U.S. dollar continues to weaken against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and investors are in risk-seeking mode, the U.S. dollar will remain under modest pressure against the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 Both the Singapore dollar and South Korean won rose sharply against the U.S. dollar Monday due to expectations that the yuan will appreciate.\par \par \uc2 Former HKMA head Joseph Yam said: "The Renminbi (yuan) exchange rate against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume a long-term appreciation trend."\par \par \uc2 But Yam said he expects short-term volatility in the yuan's exchange rate against the U.S. dollar due to the uncertainty in the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial markets.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2331; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 21-06-10 0840GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100621e66l000p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
