\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dollar Higher Late On Inflows; Likely To Stay Strong\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Latest     Change \par USD/HKD Spot              7.7641     -0.0004 \par 1-year USD/HKD Forward*   -193       Unchanged \par Overnight Hibor           0.26%      Unchanged \par 1-month Hibor             0.26%      Unchanged \par 3-month Hibor             0.10%      +1 bp \par 1-year Hibor              0.55%      Unchanged \par 2-year EF Note            0.75%      +3 bps \par 10-year EF Note           2.77%      +3 bps \par  \par *mid-point of bid-offer spread \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong rose against the U.S. dollar late Tuesday, as funds flowed into Asia amid easing concerns over Greece's debt problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said demand for the Hong Kong dollar will remain strong, although its strength will be offset by low returns as the local unit will track the ultra-low U.S. interest rate because of its peg to the U.S. dollar. The U.S. dollar will likely stay in its current range of HK$7.7620-HK$7.7660 this week.\par \par \uc2 In late Asian trade, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.7641, down from HK$7.7645 late Monday. The U.S. unit was fixed at HK$7.7634 earlier Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Given the HKMA (\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) by default doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits HK$7.7500, some funds still prefer \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  as many Asian central banks actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at whatever level they wish," a trader from a U.K. bank said.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Hong Kong dollar is largely in sync with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, highlighting the fact that inflows to the whole Asian region is very strong for the moment," a trader from another U.K. bank said.\par \par \uc2 The one-year U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forward contract was quoted at a discount of 193 points to the spot rate, unchanged from late Monday.\par \par \uc2 -By Aries Poon, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832-2332; aries.poon@dowjones.com [ 30-03-10 0815GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1053 4178   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100330e63u000pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
