\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar at 15-mth low on China policy concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2010\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Jan 18 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0500 GMT     At 0609 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7607/08        7.7583/85\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>      -50/-46          -52/-49\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -98/-92          -104/-99\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -198/-188        -230/-185\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.01/0.51        0.01/0.51\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.01/0.51        0.02/0.11\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.02/0.12        0.02/0.22\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.01/0.51        0.07/0.34\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.39/0.54        0.39/0.51\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2  * The Hong Kong dollar weakened to a 15-month low of 7.7625 to the U.S. dollar on Monday on concern that capital inflows from China could ease if the Beijing authorities continue to tighten monetary policy, and there was no sign of hot money inflows from elsewhere for the time being.\par \par \uc2  "If China persistently tightens its monetary policy forcing Chinese banks to repatriate funds back to the mainland, capital inflows from the mainland (to Hong Kong) will definitely come down and that could further weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a regional bank. "The next move (of the Hong Kong dollar) will be dictated by fund flows."\par \par \uc2  China signalled a tighter policy stance last week by raising bank reserve requirements. Tighter liquidity could curb the flow of money into Hong Kong from the mainland, which has been massive in the past year due to a low interest rate environment and Beijing's economic stimulus package.\par \par \uc2  * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was quoted at 7.7607/08 versus the U.S. dollar at 0501 GMT, having earlier hit 7.7625, its lowest level since mid-October 2008.\par \par \uc2  * A record HK$640 billion (US$83 billion) in funds flowed into Hong Kong between October 2008 and December 2009, much of them from mainland China, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in a bid to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2  * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2  * Local interbank rates were trapped in a narrow band on Monday with three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> fixed at 0.12000 percent, unchanged from Friday. One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.53929 percent, compared with 0.54929 percent the previous day.\par \par \uc2  MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Donny Kwok; editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \p