\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar at 10-month low on China policy concern\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2010\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0609 GMT      At 0553 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7583/85        7.7567/69\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>        -52/-49    -51.50/-47.50\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>         -104/-99    -102.50/-92.50\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -230/-185        -215/-205\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.01/0.51        0.01/0.15\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.11        0.02/0.11\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.02/0.22        0.03/0.33\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.07/0.34        0.07/0.34\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.39/0.51        0.60/1.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar weakened to a 10-month low at 7.7588 to the U.S. dollar on Friday on persistent fears that capital inflows could ease if China continues to tighten monetary policy. As risk appetite continued to improve along with global economic data, investors were also using funds parked in Hong Kong to invest in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets elsewhere in Asia, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 China signalled a tighter policy stance this week by raising bank reserve requirements. Tighter liquidity on the mainland could curb the flow of money into Hong Kong from the mainland, which has been massive in the past year as low interest rates and Beijing's economic stimulus package have created excess liquidity.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was quoted at 7.7583/84 versus the U.S. dollar at 0632 GMT, having earlier hit 7.7588, its lowest level since early March last year.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong attracted a record HK$640 billion (US$83 billion) in fund inflows between October 2008 and December 2009, much of it from mainland China and forcing massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates remained trapped in a narrow range on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.12000 percent, unchanged from Thursday. One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.06000, compared with 0.05964 percent the previous day.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Susan Fenton; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100118e61f000fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
