\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar eases slightly as stocks slide\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2010\par 07:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0553 GMT      At 0515 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7551/52        7.7547/48\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -50/-46          -52/-49\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -102/-94         -105/-100\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -210/-200        -220/-210\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001/0.03     0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.01/0.06        0.01/0.06\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.07/0.12        0.07/0.12\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.24        0.20/0.24\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.50/0.55        0.50/0.56\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar was a tad weaker against the U.S. dollar, with sentiment hurt by a plunge in the domestic stock market after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would raise banks' reserve requirements to cool rampant credit and investment growth in the world's third-largest economy. [ID:nTOE60B095]\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was quoted at 7.7551 versus the U.S. dollar at 0553 GMT, having earlier hit a session low of 7.7556.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was down 2.24 percent at the midday break, while the China Enterprise Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks had lost 3.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 * "There is a risk of capital outflow if the stock market continues to fall as investors fear more austerity measures from China in the near future," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 But another trader believed heavy capital outflows from Hong Kong were unlikely because some long-term investors were seeking exposure to China's growth.\par \par \uc2 He projected the Hong Kong dollar would trade in a range between 7.7550 and 7.7585 in the next two weeks.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong attracted a record HK$640 billion in fund inflows between October 2008 and December 2009, forcing massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were trapped in a narrow range on Wednesday in quiet trade, said a dealer at a regional bank.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.12000 percent, unchanged from Tuesday. One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> softened to 0.54929 percent from 0.56000 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PC