\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar eases slightly, interbank rates remain low\b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2009\par 07:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0549 GMT      At 0526 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7507/08        7.7505/06\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -63/-59          -60/-56\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -125/-120        -124/-118\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -265/-258        -265/-255\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.0001          0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.05        0.02/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.06/0.10        0.06/0.11\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.15/0.23        0.15/0.24\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.45/0.53        0.50/0.54\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar edged lower but stayed in a narrow range on Friday amid corporate demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while interbank rates remained soft as the banking system was flush with liquidity.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was quoted at 7.7507 at 0612 GMT, after hitting a three-month low of 7.7510 in early trade, but was still near the upper end of its tight band to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers attributed the modest fall to year-end position adjustment and on corporate demand for U.S. dollar funding.\par \par \uc2 A trader at a local bank expected the Hong Kong dollar to remain supported, given a rebound in the domestic stock market and positive data from China signalling the world's third-largest economy is on a steady growth track.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks rose on Friday, recovering from five days of losses, with the Hang Seng Index <.HSI> gaining 1.68 percent and the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks up 1.55 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong attracted strong capital inflows this year as investors were optimistic about China's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 * China's industrial growth in November accelerated to 19.2 percent from a year earlier, its highest since June 2007, while investment expansion remain robust. [ID:nECONCN]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were steady to a touch lower because of abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10036 percent, softening from Thursday's 0.10821 percent.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing\par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- stood at HK$303.597\par billion on Friday.\par  MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Ken Wills)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 