\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar steady, stock market in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2009\par 07:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 10 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0526 GMT      At 0442 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7505/06        7.7506/07\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -60/-56          -59/-54\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -124/-118        -119/-114\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -265/-255        -263/-248\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001/0.03     0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.05        0.02/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.06/0.11        0.06/0.11\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.15/0.24        0.20/0.25\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.50/0.54        0.50/0.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar held within a narrow range against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, with attention focusing on moves in the stock market and fund flows.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> traded between 7.7503 and 7.7506 near the upper end of its tight band to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 * "There is a risk of capital outflow if the stock market continues to fall as investors may take profits after the stock index gained sharply so far this year," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks opened higher on Thursday, rebounding from four days of losses, but then dipped into negative territory. The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was down 0.76 percent, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks fell 1.12 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * A flood of fund inflow into Hong Kong has pushed the stock market 50 percent higher this year and the residential property prices rose 30 percent.\par \par \uc2 The influx of capital is putting the Hong Kong dollar under pressure and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 A total of HK$463.4 billion fund flowed into Hong Kong between March 20 and Dec. 4, 2009.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates remained at low levels due to abundant liquidity in the banking system after strong capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10821 percent, easing from Wednesday's 0.10893 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091213e5ca00026\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
