\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr moves in tight range; interbank rates mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2009\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0549 GMT      At 0515 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -60/-57         -58/-55\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -126/-120       -119/-112\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -267/-257       -253/-245\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001/0.03    0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.04/0.05       0.02/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.06/0.11       0.06/0.10\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.26       0.20/0.25\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.50/0.59       0.44/0.54\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar moved narrowly near the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar, while local interbank rates were mixed with longer-dated rates tracking U.S. rates higher after upbeat U.S. jobs data in November.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> traded between 7.7500 and 7.7503 to the U.S. dollar during the session, barely changed from Friday's rate.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers expected the spot rate <HKD=> to hover at the current levels, closing at the upper end of the trading band at 7.75 against the U.S. dollar, as a steady stream of initial public offerings in the stock market may draw investment fund inflows. Speculation that China could soon resume appreciation of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CNY=CFXS> is also putting attention on the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is often seen as a proxy for the Chinese yuan.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China Pacific Insurance (Group) Co Ltd\uc2 , the country's third-largest life insurer, plans to raise up to HK$25.9 billion ($3.34 billion) from a Hong Kong IPO, a source to the deal said. [ID:nHKG490511]\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over recent months to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising beyond its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice and sold a total of HK$5.425 billion ($700 million) for U.S. dollar during the Asian and New York trading session. [ID:nHKG485458]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were mixed.\par \par \uc2 Short-dated rates remained at low levels because of abundant liquidity in the banking system after HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10857 percent, down from Friday's 0.10893 percent.\par \par \uc2 But longer-dated interbank rates were marked higher, taking a lead from a rise in Hong Kong dollar interest rate swaps (IRS) after a jump in U.S. bond yields on Friday, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.58286 percent, up from the previous session's 0.54000 percent.\par \par \uc2 A dealer said market players were adjusting positions and actual dealing in the longer-dated interbank rates had been thin.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury debt prices tumbled on Friday, sending yields to three-week highs, as data showing a surprisingly small number of U.S. job losses in November fuelled economic recovery hope and stoked speculation that the Federal Reserve may consider raising interest rates sooner than previously thought. [US/]\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > HK "very concerned" about asset bubble risk   [ID:nTOE5B604I]\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091210e5c7000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
