\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar stays firm despite weak stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2009\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 4 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0515 GMT      At 0501 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -58/-55          -58/-55\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -119/-112        -118/-113\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -253/-245        -248/-238\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001/0.03     0.0001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.05        0.01/0.02\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.06/0.10        0.05/0.08\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.25        0.20/0.23\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.44/0.54        0.45/0.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar held steady at the top end of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Friday, despite a pullback in the stock market after recent sharp gains.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers expected the spot exchange rate <HKD=> to stay in a narrow range ahead of the release of a key U.S. jobs data later in the day.\par \par \uc2 However, dealers said the Hong Kong dollar was likely to remain supported by inflows of funds from overseas investors who are optimistic about the economic rebound in Asia.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday afternoon and sold HK$3.875 billion ($500 million) for U.S. dollars to steam a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep it within its fixed trading band. [ID:nHKG201044]\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks fell on Friday, snapping a four-day rally, tracking weaker overseas markets after soft U.S. data raised concern over the pace of recovery in the world's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was down 1.39 percent, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks shed 1.56 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank offered rates <HIBOR=> were fixed a touch firmer than the previous session, but remained at a low level as the banking system was flush with liquidity following frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA over recent months to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg amid capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10893 percent, inching up from Thursday's 0.10821 percent.\par \par \uc2 * Market participants are looking ahead to U.S. non-farm payrolls data due at 1330 GMT, for fresh trading clues.\par \par \uc2 Economists in a Reuters survey forecast 130,000 U.S. jobs were lost in November compared with a loss of 190,000 jobs in October. The U.S. unemployment rate is expected to remain the same at 10.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) ((christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +852 2843 6960; Reuters Messaging:christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) (Multimedia versions of Reuters Top News are now available for:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * 3000 Xtra: visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.session.rservices.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.session.rservices.com}}}\uc2 \f2  * BridgeStation: view story .134 For more information on TopNews, please visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ))\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For more information on Top News, visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 <REUTER> <HONG KONG>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hong Kong news        [HK]     Hong Kong stock report [.HSI]\par  China news            [CN]     Hong Kong hot stocks [HK-HOT]\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   [FRX]    Hong Kong diary    [HK/DIARY]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Press digests [PRESS/HK]\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091207e5c40007a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
