\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar stays firm, market eyes fund flows\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 06:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0501 GMT      At 0559 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -58/-55          -59/-55\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -118/-113        -122/-114\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -248/-238        -253/-243\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.0001           0.00001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.01/0.02        0.01/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.05/0.08        0.05/0.10\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.23        0.20/0.24\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.45/0.50        0.42/0.52\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar was stuck at the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, with sentiment buoyed by extended gains in the domestic stock market.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks rose for a fourth straight session on Thursday, with the Hang Seng Index <.HSI> gaining 0.62 percent and the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks up 0.67 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers expected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> to remain strong as the territory continued to draw fund flows from investors seeking exposure to China's growth.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank offered rates (HIBOR=) were fixed slightly higher than the previous session.\par \par \uc2 But dealers said the prices were trading much lower than the fixing rates because the market was awash with liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The three-month interbank rate was quoted at 0.05/0.08 percent versus the fixing rate <HIHKD3MD=> at 0.10821 percent.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity has remained flush in the local interbank market following frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) over recent months in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg amid strong capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing\par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- stood at HK$302.956\par billion on Thursday.\par  MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) ((christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +852 2843 6960; Reuters Messaging:christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) (Multimedia versions of Reuters Top News are now available for:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * 3000 Xtra: visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.session.rservices.com