\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dollar Flat Late Despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Inflows Continue\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2009\par 09:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Latest     Change \par USD/HKD Spot              7.7501     Unchanged \par 1-year USD/HKD Forward*   -245       +2 \par Overnight Hibor           0.26%      +18 bps \par 1-month Hibor             0.26%      +18 bps \par 3-month Hibor             0.17%      +6 bps \par 1-year Hibor              0.43%      -4 bps \par 2-year EF Note            0.38%      +10 bps \par 10-year EF Note           2.17%      +2 bps \par  \par *mid-point of bid-offer spread \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar was steady near the upper limit of its trading band against the U.S. dollar Thursday, as further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to be offset by fund inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Hong Kong dollar is likely to hover around the current level for the rest of the year as inflows persist. They said they expect the U.S. dollar to stay in a tight range between HK$7.7500 and HK$7.7503 Friday.\par \par \uc2 In late Asian trade, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.7501, steady from late Wednesday. The U.S. unit was fixed at HK$7.7501 earlier Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Although we may be seeing some investor fatigue, as inflows have slowed a bit recently and the stock market rose less aggressively today, the flows are still considered strong and will probably keep the Hong Kong dollar strong," said a trader at a local bank.\par \par \uc2 The inflows prompted the city's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell HK$3.88 billion Thursday to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the strong side of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Hong Kong's positive economic outlook will likely lure more funds to the city.\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund said in a report Thursday that it expects Hong Kong's economy to continue to grow steadily, though the recovery remains fragile.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  on Thursday raised its 2010 forecast for Hong Kong's gross domestic product growth to 5.8% from 5.0%.\par \par \uc2 The one-year U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forward contract was quoted at a discount of 245 points to the spot rate, compared with a 247-point discount late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 03-12-09 0824GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1053 4178   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091203e5c3000m4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
