\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hovers at upper limit,eyes on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2009\par 07:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0559 GMT      At 0531 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7501/02\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -59/-55          -62/-59\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -122/-114        -128/-122\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -253/-243        -258/-248\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001          0.00001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.01/0.05        0.005/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.05/0.10        0.05/0.10\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.24        0.20/0.25\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.42/0.52        0.43/0.53\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar traded back at the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, with sentiment boosted by extended gains in the domestic stock market and signs of an improving global economy.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks rose for a third straight day on Wednesday as concerns over Dubai debt problems receded and positive U.S. home sales data restored confidence in a global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was up 1.28 percent, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks surged 1.64 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers expected the Hong Kong dollar will continue to hover at the current level, with the prospect of more funds flowing into the territory as recent data provided more evidence that the local economy is recovering.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong retail sales in October rose from a year earlier for a second straight month, by 9.8 percent and at a much faster pace, government data showed on Tuesday. [ID:nHKG30847]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were steady to a tad lower on Wednesday because of abundant liquidity in the banking system following frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA over recent months to \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg amid strong capital inflows..\par    Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> stayed at 0.10000 percent,\par its lowest level since February 2004.\par    One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.51857 percent,\par down from 0.52929 percent on Tuesday and down 25 basis points\par from rates a month earlier.\par    The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing\par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- stood at HK$302.956\par billion on Wednesday.\par  MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Ken Wills) ((christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +852 2843 6960; Reuters Messaging:christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) (Multimedia versions of Reuters Top News are now available for:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * 3000 Xtra: visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.session.rservices.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.session.rservices.com}}}\uc2 \f2  * BridgeStation: view story .134 For more information on TopNews, please visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ))\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For more information on Top News, visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 <REUTER> <HONG KONG>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hong Kong news        [HK]     Hong Kong stock report [.HSI]\par  China news            [CN]     Hong Kong hot stocks [HK-HOT]\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   [FRX]    Hong Kong diary    [HK/DIARY]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Press digests [PRESS/HK]\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091205e5c200030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
