\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar recovers ground as Dubai concerns ease\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2009\par 07:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0531 GMT      At 0539 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7501/02        7.7502/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -62/-59         -57/-52\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -128/-122       -114/-106\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -258/-248       -240/-220\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001         0.00001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.005/0.05      0.02/0.05\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.05/0.10       0.05/0.10\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.25       0.20/0.23\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.43/0.53       0.45/0.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar moved in a narrow range on Tuesday, consolidating after it hit a two-month low against the U.S. dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 * One dealer at a local bank said demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dwindled, with sentiment lifted by a rally in the stock market.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> traded between 7.7500 and 7.7502 on Tuesday, recovering from Monday's low of 7.7506 versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar had weakened on Monday morning as dealers said some foreign banks were repatriating funds back to their home countries amid concern about the potential fallout from Dubai's debt problems.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks extended gains on Tuesday as concerns over Dubai crisis eased sending banking shares higher.\par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was up 0.55 percent, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks rose 1 percent at the midday break.\par \par \uc2 * Dubai World, the holding company at the heart of the Dubai crisis, on Monday announced a restructuring plan involving $26 billion in debt. However, the Dubai government said it was not responsible for the debts of Dubai World, dealing a blow to creditors' assumptions that the Arab emirate would guarantee the conglomerate's liabilities. [ID:nGEE5AT1SZ]\par \par \uc2 * Some dealers expected the USD/HKD spot rate to trade in a narrow range of 7.7500-7.7505 in the next few days, as they eyed U.S. economic data due later this week for fresh trading cues.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates extended their decline on Tuesday because of abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10000 percent, its lowest level since February 2004, and it was down 8 basis point in the past month.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong government will release retail sales data for October at 0830 GMT.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting 