\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hit a two-month low on Dubai jitters\b0\par\par\uc2 747 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2009\par 07:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0539 GMT      At 0519 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7502/03        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -57/-52          -53/-50\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -114/-106        -103/-98\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -240/-220        -223/-213\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001          0.00001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.02/0.05        0.005/0.06\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.05/0.10        0.03/0.11\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.23        0.20/0.28\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.45/0.55        0.50/0.56\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar weakened against the U.S. dollar on Monday, hitting its lowest level in two months, with some dealers saying some foreign banks were repatriating funds back to their home countries amid concern about the potential fall-out from Dubai's debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> dropped to as low as 7.7506, its weakest level since late September, Reuters data showed. It was quoted at 7.7502/03 versus the U.S. dollar at 0539 GMT.\par \par \uc2 * One dealer said there was some bidding interest in the U.S. dollar by U.K. and U.S. banks and he suspected the move might be related to Dubai's woes.\par \par \uc2 Some banks, which have exposure to the Dubai debt crises, may need to repatriate some funds back to their headquarters, another trader said.\par \par \uc2 * Financial markets were rattled last week after Dubai said it would ask creditors of Dubai World and property group Nakheel to agree a standstill on debt payments as part of a restructuring. [ID:nGEE5A02FN]\par \par \uc2 The United Arab Emirates' \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set up an emergency facility on Sunday to support bank liquidity in the first policy response to Dubai's debt woes, which had threatened to paralyse lending and derail economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 * However, dealers said they had not seen massive capital outflows from Hong Kong. One dealer expected the spot rate to trade in a range of 7.7500-7.7515 this week.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that the financial problems of Dubai World should not pose any systemic risk to the Hong Kong banking sector, as the lenders' total exposure to the United Arab Emirates, of which Dubai is a member, amounted to only 0.39 percent of their total assets as at the end of September 2009. [ID:nHKG10210]\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks rebounded on Monday with banking shares recovering from steep losses last Friday on Dubai's debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was up 3.29 percent at the midday break, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks climbed 4.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates continued to decline on Monday because of abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.10107 percent, down from Friday's 0.10964.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) ((christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +852 2843 6960; Reuters Messaging:christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net)) ((If you have a query or comment on this story, send an email to news.feedback.asia@thomsonreuters.com)) (Multimedia versions of Reuters Top News are now available for:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * 3000 Xtra: visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.session.rservices.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.session.rservices.com}}}\uc2 \f2  * BridgeStation: view story .134 For more information on TopNews, please visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ))\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For more information on Top News, visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://topnews.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://topnews.reuters.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 <REUTER> <HONG KONG>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hong Kong news        [HK]     Hong Kong stock report [.HSI]\par  China news            [CN]     Hong Kong hot stocks [HK-HOT]\par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   [FRX]    Hong Kong diary    [HK/DIARY]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Press digests [PRESS/HK]\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091203e5bu000ae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pic