\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar in a tight range, market eyes fund flows\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 06:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Nov 27 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0519 GMT      At 0500 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -53/-50          -49/-45\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -103/-98         -102/-96\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -223/-213        -225/-215\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.00001/0.03     0.0001/0.01\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.005/0.06       0.005/0.06\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.03/0.11        0.06/0.11\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.20/0.28        0.20/0.29\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.50/0.56        0.50/0.57\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2  * The Hong Kong dollar moved in a narrow range between 7.7500 and 7.7503 against the U.S. dollar on Friday, and some dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might weaken slightly in the near term as capital inflows slowed amid a falling stock market.\par \par \uc2  * Hong Kong stocks plunged on Friday as concerns about Dubai's debt problems dragged down banking shares. The Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was down 3.45 percent at the midday break, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top locally listed mainland Chinese stocks shed 3.58 percent.\par \par \uc2    Dubai said on Wednesday it would ask creditors of Dubai World and property group Nakheel to agree a standstill on $59 billion in debt as a first step towards restructuring. [ID:nGEE5A02L1]\par \par \uc2  * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> has gained support over recent months on strong capital inflows into stock and property markets.\par \par \uc2  * One dealer projected the USD/HKD spot rate to trade in a narrow range of 7.7500-7.7510, saying investors would likely to keep their funds in Hong Kong amid optimism over China's economic growth and expectations that the yuan <CNY=CFXS> will continue to appreciate.\par \par \uc2  * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2  * Local interbank rates remained at low level because of abundant liquidity in the banking system following frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2   Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> stayed at 0.10964 percent, its lowest since mid-February, 2004.\par \par \uc2   The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA - stood at HK$318.009 billion.\par \par \uc2  MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Christina Lo)\par  ((christina.lo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +852 2843 6960; Reuters\par Messagi