\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Sells HK$4.28B In NY Trade Friday To Defend US Dollar Peg\b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2009\par 06:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$4.28 billion in the New York trading session Friday to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 This follows four overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of HK$21.3 billion, bringing the HKMA's total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to HK$25.575 billion.\par \par \uc2 The latest injection increases \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggregate balance to HK$315.29 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the strong side of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 At 0545 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at HK$7.75, flat from late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85\par \par \uc2 -By Yvonne Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; yvonne.lee@dowjones.com [ 14-11-09 0553GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091114e5be0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
