\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS-Aussie swaps up as rate expectations build\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2009\par 09:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Greater chance seen for more Australia rate increases\par \par \uc2  * Hong Kong aggregate balance at record high\par \par \uc2  * Dollar borrowing cost at new trough\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Nov 13 (Reuters) - Australian swaps rose on Friday as investors grew increasing certain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates at its Dec. 1 policy meeting after positive employment data supported the case for monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  is seen raising interest rates by 25 basis points to 3.75 percent as part of a policy tightening campaign expected to run through 2010. A Reuters poll showed 15 out of 18 respondents expect such a move. [ID:nSYD33220]\par \par \uc2  On Thursday, data showed Australian employment rose 24,500 in October, a second month of surprisingly strong growth.\par \par \uc2  One-year swap rates <AUDQM3AB1Y=> rose 3 basis points (bps) to 4.74 percent while the one-month overnight indexed swaps <AUD1MOIS=> rose 2 bps to 3.5825 percent.\par \par \uc2  But the rates market has still not fully priced in a rate increase, preferring to wait for Tuesday's release of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minutes.\par \par \uc2  It is still seeing only an 84 percent chance the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten by 25 basis points <CSRBA=CSAU> next month, but that is higher than 68 percent at the start of the week.\par \par \uc2  "The market is underpriced for a December tightening," said Annette Beacher, senior Strategist at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "Tuesday's the last chance for the RBA to communicate they didn't mean to suggest a pause. We are saying yes for another 25 bps increase in rates," Beacher said.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already raised rates by 25 basis points in both October and November, becoming the first in the G20 to tighten since the global credit crisis blew up. If the RBA hikes rates in December, it would be the first time it would have tightened three months in a row.\par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 , interbank rates continued to decline as repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market injected increased liquidity in the domestic banking system.\par \par \uc2  One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.63929 percent, down from Thursday's 0.64929 percent. It has fallen 9 basis points this week. Short-dated interbank rates continue to hover around zero.\par \par \uc2  Money is flowing into Hong Kong ahead of big upcoming IPOs in the territory, including a jumbo $4 billion offering by China's seventh-biggest bank \uc2 China Minsheng Banking Corp\uc2  .\par \par \uc2  Since October, the HKMA has injected more than HK$140 billion in the territory's banking system to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, including Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  As a result, the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- will increase to a record HK$294.368 billion by Nov. 17 when the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is settled.\par \par \uc2  The borrowing cost of dollars continued to fall in Asia after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council Member Michael Bonello told Reuters on Thursday the bank would ensure pulling back its liquidity lifeline did not disrupt markets. [ID:nLAG005916]\par \par \uc2  In Singapore, 3-month dollars <SIUSDD=ABSG> are quoted at an average 0.27607 percent, a fresh low.    (Reporting by Umesh Desai; Editing by Kim Coghill)    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY/ (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|U|NAT|J|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091113e5bd00149\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
