\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-Hong Kong dollar stays firm amid capital inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2009\par 07:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects para 4 of text to read total HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October was $11.05 billion, not $85.6 billion)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0550 GMT      At 0600 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -46/-43          -46/-42\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -103/-97         -102/-96\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -220/-214        -222/-213\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.005/0.05       0.005/0.05\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.05/0.11        0.05/0.11\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.11/0.16        0.12/0.17\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.30/0.41        0.32/0.42\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.60/0.69        0.60/0.70\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar held at the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, prompting the city's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in and sell HK$5.425 billion ($700 million) for U.S. dollars in late morning to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg, amid a persistent inflow of funds into the territory. [ID:nHKG194184]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Some dealers said they expect further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) because there are several IPOs in the stock market which may draw investment fund inflows into the city, while the U.S. dollar remains weak in view of the fact that the Federal Reserve will keep interest rates near zero for some time.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The HKMA has been actively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly hit its upper trading limit at 7.7500 to the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data on Monday showed that Hong Kong's official foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve assets jumped by $13.2 billion in October from September to a record $240.1 billion. That was the biggest monthly increase this year as the HKMA bought $11.05 billion during the month to keep the Hong Kong dollar within its trading band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far this month, the HKMA has injected a total of HK$30.225 billion into the territory's banking system to keep the trading band intact, including Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  As a result, the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances\par on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 projected to increase to HK$269.92 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The HKMA is usually obliged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Local interbank rates remained at low levels because of abundant liquidity in the banking system, and on the expectation that U.S. interest rates were likely to stay near zero for a while.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.15964 percent, a five-year low, and down from Monday's 0.16750 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, two-week Hibor <HIHKD2WD> nudged higher to 0.08786 percent from the previous session's 0.07786 percent on IPO-related fund demand, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS > Stock market reports and updates: [.HK] > Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/] > U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/] > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX] (Reporting by Christina Lo and Susan Fenton; Editing by Ken Wills)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091113e5ba000nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
