\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: HKMA October  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Hit Peak For Year\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2009\par 12:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds value of HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October hit monthly peak for this year.)\par \par \uc2 By Chester Yung and Aries Poon\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October has hit a peak for the year, as the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defends the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of a continued influx of foreign funds into Asia.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA has sold about HK$74 billion to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this month. The total surpassed May's figure, when the HKMA sold HK$73.78 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Bolstered by the strong start to the third-quarter earnings season, foreign investors have poured funds into Asia on expectations of increased U.S. and European demand for commodity and other exports from emerging markets, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Traders said there is no indication the Hong Kong dollar will weaken before the end of the year and they expect more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA. At 1002 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at HK$7.7502.\par \par \uc2 "The local property and stock markets are still holding firm. There is no incentive to push investors out of Hong Kong," said a trader with a U.K. bank.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA has injected HK$27.13 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so far this week. The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the strong side of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band. Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year have pushed the aggregate balance, a measure of commercial banks' clearing and reserve account holdings with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to HK$235.60 billion.\par \par \uc2 According to fund tracker EPFR Global, the amount of funds dedicated to emerging-market stocks totaled US$4.03 billion in the week ended Oct. 14, its highest level this year. The region's bond markets also absorbed US$967 million worth of new funds over that week. Separate data on inflows into Hong Kong were not available.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong is one of the preferred destinations for funds in the region, traders and fund managers said, adding demand for shares of locally listed Chinese heavyweights such as \uc2 Industrial & Commercial Bank of China\uc2  and \uc2 PetroChina\uc2  is strong among foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Hang Seng Index has been hovering above the psychological 20,000 level since Sept. 3, and hit a 14-month intraday high of 22,620.01 Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Traders said investors' expectations the Chinese yuan will appreciate on the back of a strong domestic economy have also lured funds to Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Law Ka-Chung, the chief economist at Bank of Communications, warned of a possible correction in the local stock market by end of the year, which could trigger capital outflows, pulling the Hong Kong dollar back from the high end of its trading band.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung and Aries Poon, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 23-10-09 1027GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1053 4178   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091023e5an0012j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
