\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar stays at top of trading band, eyes on HKMA\b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2009\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Oct 16 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0600 GMT      At 0458 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7500/01        7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -45/-43          -46/-43\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>         -98/-90          -97/-92\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -188/-178        -185/-175\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.0001/0.05      0.00001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.05/0.11        0.02/0.10\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.12/0.21        0.08/0.20\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.40/0.51        0.40/0.50\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0/80/0.84        0.75/0.83\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar held at the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Friday, with signs of continuous funds flowing into the territory.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers said they expect further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) as global markets remain awash with liquidity, while interest rates remain low. Capital has been flowing into Asia on optimism about the region's economic recovery, as well as expectations that the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> will continue to appreciate.\par \par \uc2 * The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, selling a total of HK$10.075 billion ($1.3 billion) for U.S. dollars to stem a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep it within its fixed trading band. [ID:nHKG95697]\par \par \uc2 So far this month, the HKMA has injected a total of HK$45.725 billion into the territory's banking system, including Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were a tad higher from the previous session as some players covered positions ahead of the weekend.\par \par \uc2 One-month Hibor <HIHKD1MD=> was fixed at 0.10714 percent, compared with Thursday's 0.10000 percent.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> rebounded slightly to 0.20571 percent from 0.19857 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said interbank rates would likely to remain low, with abundant liquidity, more than HK$210 billion, parked in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091019e5ag000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
