\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA sells HK$4.65 bln in NY trade to keep HK dlr in band\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2009\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Oct 16 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , injected HK$4.65 billion (US$600 million) into the money market in New York trade on Thursday, in addition to its earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, to stem an appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <HKD=> and keep it within its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 In total, the HKMA sold HK$10.075 billion for U.S. dollars in Hong Kong and New York on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has repeatedly hit the top of its trading band at 7.7500 in recent weeks as its peg to a weak U.S. dollar is encouraging fund flows into Hong Kong assets, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 According to data on Reuters page <HKMAOOC>, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$217.175 billion by Oct. 20.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Under the linked exchange rate mechanism, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the trading band in tact if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85. (Reporting by Susan Fenton, Editing by Ken Wills)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091016e5ag00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\p