vious day. [FRX/]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local curency hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local longer-dated interbank rates and interest rate swaps (IRS) nudged higher, taking a cue from a rise in U.S. bond yields overnight, dealers said. [US/]\par \par \uc2 One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> was fixed at 0.84500 percent, up from Tuesday's 0.82929 percent.\par \par \uc2 One-year IRS rose to 0.52 percent from 0. 0.502 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091010e5a70002m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
