\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar edges lower, but stuck in a tight range\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2009\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                            Latest           Previous Day\par                            At 0554 GMT      At 0600 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>           7.7506/07        7.7502/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>       -55/-53          -56/-53\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>        -111/-106        -111/-106\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>         -197/-187        -200/-190\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>       0.20/0.25        0.25/0.25\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>       0.10/0.14        0.10/0.14\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=>     0.13/0.21        0.11/0.21\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>       0.40/0.50        0.40/0.50\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>        0.80/0.88        0.77/0.87\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <HKDF=>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar edged lower against the U.S. dollar on Monday but trading was confined to a narrow range.\par \par \uc2 "Buying orders for the Hong Kong dollar have been slowing down after the closure of the subscription for the biggest IPOs," said a dealer at a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Applications for the share offering of \uc2 Sinopharm Group Co Ltd\uc2  and \uc2 Metallurgical Corp of China\uc2  closed last week, with heavy oversubscription by investors.\par \par \uc2 * Another dealer attributed the modest fall to some commercial demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He expected the spot rate <HKD=> to stay in a narrow range of 7.7500-7.7515 in the near term, with attention focusing on fund flows and a string of ongoing IPOs.\par \par \uc2 About seven companies are expected to list on the Hong Kong bourse in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 * Chinese real estate developer Glorious Property hopes to raise over $1.5 billion in a Hong Kong IPO, while \uc2 China Resources Cement Holdings Ltd\uc2  is seeking to raise up to $824 million. Both companies opened their retail books on Monday. [ID:nHKG99147] [ID:nHKG216973]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates moved in a tight range.\par \par \uc2 One-week Hibor <HIHKD1WD=> was fixed at 0.17929 percent, softening from Friday's 0.19714 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said short-dated rates were expected to ease further later this week when more money is released from heavily oversubscribed IPOs.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Sinopharm Group will begin trading on Sept. 23, while the trading debut for Metallurgical Corp is scheduled on Sept. 24.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards were little changed in quiet trade.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090924e59l000bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40