\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar firms slightly, buoyed by stock market gains\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2009\par 06:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Aug 24 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Latest       Previous Close\par                       At 0350 GMT  At 0852 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7507/08    7.7512/13\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>  -68/-63      -65/-61\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>   -126/-116    -120/-115\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>    -207/-197    -197/-185\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=> 0.00005/0.03  0.0001/0.03\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.03/0.08   0.03/0.08\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.13/0.22   0.13/0.22\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.42/0.52   0.40/0.52\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    0.80/0.90   0.80/0.89\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar nudged higher against the U.S. dollar on Monday, due in part to a rally in the stock market lifting sentiment.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> firmed to 7.7507/08 near the upper end of its tight band against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 * Asian stock markets climbed on Monday after upbeat U.S. housing data and positive comments by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke. [ID:nSP383049]\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index <.HSI> was up 1.90 percent at 0354 GMT, while the China Enterprises Index <.HSCE> of top mainland companies had advanced 2.15 percent.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates traded narrowly mixed.\par \par \uc2 Short-dated rates remained at low levels as the banking system was flush with liquidity, following frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months to curb the strength of the Hong Kong dollar amid capital inflows into the territory.\par \par \uc2 The overnight rate stayed at near zero. Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.21714 percent, its lowest level since early November 2004, and down from Friday's 0.21857 percent.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing\par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- stood at\par HK$211.368 billion on Monday.\par    But longer-dated interbank rates edged up from the\par previous session, taking a lead from a rise in Hong Kong dollar\par interest rate swaps (IRS) after a jump in U.S. bond yields last\par Friday, dealers said.\par    One-year Hibor <HIHKD1YD=> rose to 0.90143 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's 0.88857 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened amid a firmer local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but trading remained thin, a dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090827e58o0006q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40