\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar eases slightly as stocks slide\b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2009\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market in late trade on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Close        Morning      Previous Close\par                       At 0904 GMT  At 0329 GMT  At 0905 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7502/03    7.7504/05    7.7501/02\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>  -71/-68      -71/-68     -72/-69\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>   -130/-125    -129/-124   -133/-128\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>    -222/-216    -223/-215   -230/-225\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.0001    0.00001/0.03  0.00001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.01/0.07   0.01/0.07   0.01/0.07\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.08/0.21   0.10/0.22   0.10/0.21\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.40/0.54   0.40/0.54   0.40/0.54\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    0.82/0.97   0.85/0.98   0.80/0.97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 More live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar moved in a narrow range between 7.7502 and 7.7505 against the U.S. dollar on Friday, and some dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to weaken slightly in the near term as capital inflows slowed and amid a correction in the stock market.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong stocks <.HSI><.HSCE> retreated on Friday, tracking losses on Shanghai market <.SSEC>, on worries the mainland authorities would take measures to curb lending.\par \par \uc2 People's Bank of China Vice-Governor Su Ning told a news conference after the Shanghai market closed on Friday that China's bank lending would slow in the second half, but that monetary policy would remain moderately loose, with fine-tuning via market tools. [ID:nPEK171632]\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> has gained support over recent months on capital inflows, partly from mainland China, a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The influx of hot money had pushed up stock and property prices in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Some investors may need to repatriate funds on the heels of a tightening in China's bank lending, the dealer added.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were little changed compared with the previous session, but remained at low levels because of abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.21786 percent on Friday morning, softening slightly from Thursday's 0.21857 percent.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing\par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- stood at HK$232.996\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The discount on long-dated Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed slightly from the previous session as some players adjusted positions on worries about capital outflow, a dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Market participants are looking ahead to U.S. non-farm payroll data due at 1230 GMT, for fresh trading clues.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists in a Reuters survey forecast 320,000 jobs were lost in July, compared with a loss of 467,000 jobs the previous month. The unemployment rate is seen at 9.6 percent, which would be the highest since June 1983. [ID:nN06351468]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \