\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  for 2nd time on Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2009\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second time on Thursday, injecting HK$3.1 billion (US$400 million) into the money market to stem an appreciating Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> and keep it within its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 By 0956 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had injected a total HK$6.975 billion into the market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar hit the top of its trading band at 7.7500 on Thursday as funds continued to pour into the territory, much of it headed for the property and stock markets, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 According to data on Reuters page <HKMAOOC>, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$228.044 billion by Aug. 3.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. Under the linked exchange rate mechanism, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the trading band intact if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 By 0957 GMT, it was quoted at 7.7500/01. (Reporting by Christina Lo; writing by Susan Fenton; Editing by Chris Lewis)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090730e57u000n0\